  description:
  - Rangifer Deers are a docile species of deer native to northern mountainous regions,
    making their appearence in VeilWood an unusual sighting. It is currently unknown
    how far out the Mist extends, but a common explanation for their presence is
    that the dense haze causes lapses in the deer's migration patterns.
  - Studies show that there exist little to no Mist-borne mutations, but more specimens
    are required to make any meaningful conclusions.
